<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Open the compiler page and paste your source code or upload a file.</li>
        <li>Pick a target language from the selector.</li>
        <li>Click Generate Pseudocode and review the output.</li>
        <li>Make small edits and recompile until the logic is clear.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="doc-callout">Tip: Keep your input clean and structured to get the best output.</div>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>How Compilation Works</h2>
    <p>Pseudocoder converts input into clean pseudocode to help you with understanding logic. It is not meant to replace full language compilors but rather for support.</p>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Input is parsed and tokenized using trees.</li>
        <li>The translator produces readable pseudocode for learning and planning.</li>
        <li>The output can be refined manually or used as a reference.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Best Practices</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Break large problems into smaller functions before compiling.</li>
        <li>Use consistent naming so output stays readable.</li>
        <li>Iterate in short cycles to isolate issues quickly.</li>
        <li>Save versions in history to compare logic changes.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li><strong>Compilation failed:</strong> Check for missing braces, invalid syntax, or mixed languages.</li>
        <li><strong>Output looks wrong:</strong> Simplify input and recompile in smaller chunks.</li>
        <li><strong>No output:</strong> Ensure you selected a language and submitted the form.</li>
        <li><strong>Slow response:</strong> Reduce file size and remove unused sections.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Shortcuts and Tips</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Use the upload option when working with large files.</li>
        <li>Copy the pseudo code to your notes before making major edits.</li>
        <li>Check the FAQ for answers to common questions.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

